      en: ["Inaugurated in 1973 for the protection of local biodiversity.", "Located 28 km from the picturesque fishing village of Camarones.", "Hosts a colony of Magellanic penguins of about 20,000 individuals.", "The red volcanic rocks have an impressive geological age.", "Ideal spot for observing gray foxes and hairy armadillos.", "Guanacos in the reserve are highly habituated to human presence.", "Includes well-marked interpretive trails to scenic viewpoints.", "Part of the Patagonia Austral Inter-jurisdictional Coastal Marine Park."],
