      en: ["Constantly hosts between 4,000 and 7,000 South American sea lions.", "Inaugurated as a wildlife reserve in the year 1971.", "Located about 60 kilometers from Viedma along the coast road.", "Includes the Marine Fauna Interpretation Center, opened in 2005.", "The cliffs serve as nesting sites for numerous seabird species.", "Orcas are frequently seen patrolling the area in search of food.", "The tidal difference reveals areas rich in intertidal biodiversity.", "Observation points allow for close-up viewing with binoculars."],
