      en: ["Created in 1997 and managed by Fundación Vida Silvestre Argentina.", "Spans over 3,200 hectares of primary rainforest habitat.", "Functions as a key corridor for jaguar movement in the region.", "Shelters over 300 species of tropical forest birds.", "Includes the Urugua-í Biological Station, an active research center.", "Protects the upper course of the Urugua-í River and its tributaries.", "New species of plants and insects have been discovered here.", "Access is limited to minimize the impact on the fragile ecosystem."],
